From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 03:35:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Merge the integration branch (bench mode, movie texture fix,
 call log, pace log) into vita-app

Brings in:
* GE recorder: read RAM and VRAM through the arena (merge fix)
* Bring-up: HLE call log with argument-read mask, PNG capture of chosen presented flips
* Bench mode: INFECTED_BENCH=flips:N[,from:F] wall-time accounting by category (guest, HLE per library, GE walk, decode, GL, present, idle), exec counters per flip, pad script from file
* Bench: SAS render, ATRAC decode and movie decode categories; report to stdout, <prefix>_BENCH_OUT and a platform sink
* GL renderer: textures that wrap the end of VRAM are gathered, not dropped (the movie picture of Infected is a 512-row texture in a 480-wide buffer at 0x04154000; the draw was skipped every flip and the movies never showed)
* Bring-up: INFECTED_PACE_LOG=N prints real against emulated time every N flips
* Audio sink: without a device the game clock drains the ring (a dump has the length of the emulated time; two channels chasing each other no longer stretch it), emulated time in the trace line
* MPEG: INFECTED_PACE_LOG prints per-movie-session real vs emulated duration

